compact.snapshot_alpha` is unset or `<= 0`. Add config/env handling consistent with existing compact keys, pass pending-source and active-snapshot byte counts into the compaction trigger, preserve ADR 0035 fold horizon/retire/rebuild semantics, and add focused unit tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_config_schema.py::CompactConfig` adds `snapshot_alpha: float = _documented(0.0, ...)` and `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` adds `_SECTIONS[\"compact\"][\"snapshot_alpha\"]` using `_as_float(..., minimum=0.0)` so env/file/CLI values are coerced and validated consistently; unset or `<= 0` preserves the existing fixed-count/backfill cadence.\n- [ ] The definition site includes the exact mechanism marker `# mechanism-ok: config_key compact.snapshot_alpha — da70-18a5-898d-47ea`.\n- [ ] When `compact.snapshot_alpha > 0`, a ticket with an active snapshot folds when pending foldable source bytes are `>= snapshot_alpha * active_snapshot_bytes`, while the existing count threshold still triggers folding.\n- [ ] First-snapshot backfill remains unchanged: foldable events with no active snapshot still fold, and zero foldable events do not.\n- [ ] ADR 0035 semantics remain intact: conservative horizon, retired source/snapshot handling, rebuild-on-stray behavior, mixed-version rollback, and no snapshot event schema change.\n- [ ] Sweep compaction and per-close trigger selection use the same adaptive decision rule.\n\n## Testing\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py -q`.\n- [ ] Run `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` before push.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Add default-off compact.snapshot_alpha typed config key and definition-site mechanism marker."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"Coerce compact.snapshot_alpha as a non-negative float."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py","reason":"Centralize adaptive byte/replay-cost compaction selection while preserving existing count/backfill arms."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"Provide sweep selection with active snapshot bytes and pending foldable source bytes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"Keep per-close trigger selection aligned with sweep selection."},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py","reason":"Regression tests for default-off, alpha threshold, first-snapshot/count-floor, and snapshot event schema invariance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_typed.py","reason":"Config default/coercion/error coverage for compact.snapshot_alpha."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py","reason":"Canonical REBAR_COMPACT_SNAPSHOT_ALPHA env and config-file coverage."},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"Document compact.snapshot_alpha operator setting."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Generated/public config reference row for compact.snapshot_alpha."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","da70-18a5-898d-47ea"],["relates_to","3739-075c-089a-4d1d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"9c3e3403-e6ff-4a52-b75c-1d7bd6d14e0a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"933f-e7d8-696a-4fbd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Implement default-off compact.snapshot_alpha","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py -q","dd_id":"default-off","dd_text":"De